# Kam

Kam is a minimal, privacy-focused desktop browser for Windows.

> Status: Beta / experimental software.

## Screenshots

![Kam home page](Screenshots/Kam-Home.png)

![Kam with five tabs](Screenshots/Kam-5-Tabs.png)

## Features

- Up to 5 tabs
- Up to 7 toolbar bookmarks
- Bookmark folders
- Bookmark import and export
- Download support
- Multiple search engine options
- Basic ad and popup blocking
- No browsing history
- Camera, microphone, geolocation, and notifications are blocked by default

## Why Kam?

Built for people who want a lightweight, simple browser without distractions.

## Privacy and Security

- No account required
- No telemetry, analytics, or crash reporting
- No cloud sync of browsing data
- Bookmarks, search settings, and window preferences are stored locally
- Uses Electron Store with a locally protected encryption key
- Web tabs run with context isolation, disabled Node.js integration, and Chromium sandboxing
- Not a VPN and does not provide full phishing or Safe Browsing protection

## Trust and transparency

Kam is currently **not open source**.

The published Windows build is unsigned, so Windows SmartScreen may show a warning when you run it. This does not automatically mean the file is malware; it means Windows cannot verify a trusted publisher signature for the application.

Kam is a small personal project provided as-is. If you prefer a fully open-source browser, you may want to use a well-known open-source alternative instead.

## Limits

- Windows only
- No Chrome Web Store extension support
- Ad blocking is basic and may not block every ad, popup, redirect, or tracker
- Kam is not intended to replace full-featured browsers

## Known Issue: Yellow Border in Fullscreen Video

Occasionally, after extended fullscreen playback on some video platforms, a thin yellow border may appear around the fullscreen video area.

**Workaround:** Minimize and restore the Kam window.

## Google sign-in

Google sign-in may occasionally fail in Kam, especially after clearing the cache and cookies. This is related to how Google handles non-Chrome browsers. If this happens, try again later or use another browser.

## Requirements

- Windows 10 or later

## Install

Download Kam 1.0.0 from the [release page](https://github.com/iliya-prs/Kam/releases/tag/v1.0.0).

Windows may show a SmartScreen warning because the app is currently unsigned.

## Uninstall

- For the installed version, open **Settings > Apps > Installed apps**, find **Kam**, and select **Uninstall**.
- For the portable version, close Kam and delete the `.exe` file or its folder.
- Local Kam data may remain after uninstalling.

